menuconfig SPINALI_TIMING
  bool "Enable GNSS time discipline"
  default n
  depends on GNSS_U_BLOX_F9P_TIMEPULSE
  depends on COUNTER_CAPTURE
  depends on PTP_CLOCK
  depends on NET_GPTP
  help
    Discipline the Ethernet MAC PTP hardware clock (PHC) to GNSS time.
    A hardware capture of the receiver TIMEPULSE edge is paired with the
    UBX-TIM-TP label of that edge and fed to a 1 Hz PI servo that steers
    the PHC, which also serves gPTP. The servo owns the announced
    grandmaster quality and the UTC/leap time properties, so the node
    advertises GNSS traceability only while it holds it.

if SPINALI_TIMING

config SPINALI_TIMING_TM_AUDIT
  bool "Enable the grandmaster absolute-accuracy audit"
  default y
  depends on GPIO
  help
    Drive a GPIO wired to the receiver EXTINT input at a precisely
    measured PHC time and compare it with the UBX-TIM-TM2 timestamp the
    receiver reports for that same edge. This measures absolute PHC
    versus GNSS error end to end through the hardware, independently of
    the discipline servo. Requires a timemark-gpios property on the
    zephyr,user devicetree node.

endif # SPINALI_TIMING
